#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/id #uuid "a2b50673-6a4f-5e64-ae16-fdce0819637e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8526" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1450$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1446$ and $0.1469$. So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n0.1446 \\mid < 0.1450 < 0.1469\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\\Phi$, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.06) \\mid < Φ(z) < Φ(-1.05)\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz \\approx \\dfrac{-1.06 + (-1.05)}{2} = -1.055\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "d1e64fae-04ef-5c7d-9bb0-e81cf06bb672" :question/math-academy-id "e-8528" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$, where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.60$.\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $\\Phi{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Z \\le z) &= 0.60 \\\\\nΦ(z) &= 0.60\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz = \\Phi^{-1} (0.60)\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p = 0.60$, and we find that\n\n$$\np = 0.60 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}(p) = 0.2533\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz = \\Phi^{-1}(0.60) = 0.2533\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "a29f1f2c-104a-53aa-ad55-0c6abde0a359" :question/math-academy-id "e-8590" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$, where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20$.\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416) = 0.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3214/Source/Images/c5f6a1ed04af60c2c69b10c15f148f83.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΦ(-0.8416) &= 0.20 \\\\\nP(Z \\le - 0.8416) &= 0.20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24cd8493-039f-5963-acd0-48a8487eb6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166087} {:answer/id #uuid "3e29c109-4f9f-5d67-a8a4-a80e08df0234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.955" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166088} {:answer/id #uuid "47a55b41-9102-5941-8890-4bef5118fc3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.855" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166089} {:answer/id #uuid "5907d7f8-437e-5ee8-aaf6-ad60460fb9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.055" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166090} {:answer/id #uuid "59599ffe-cd83-5483-9a72-cfb0b1b5a829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.965" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e29c109-4f9f-5d67-a8a4-a80e08df0234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.955" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166088} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1403549-c546-5dfa-af76-838ad5ba5559" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166086}] :question/id #uuid "e5650060-a5d4-5dd4-9f6c-28e1faca58f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96869" :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\le z) = 0.1700$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $0.05$ | $0.06$ | $0.07$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-1.0$ | $0.1469$ | $0.1446$ | $0.1423$ |\n| $-0.9$ | $0.1711$ | $0.1685$ | $0.1660$ |\n| $-0.8$ | $0.1977$ | $0.1949$ | $0.1922$ |" :question/requires-calculator true}]}
